# Move the arm to a resting pose, optionally de-energising it afterwards.

# Request
# Which resting pose:
#   "safe" (default) — the taught standby pose (roboarm_ik teach_safe).
#   "zero"           — all six joints at 0 (roboarm_ik reset / init_joints_deg).
# Both put link6 around z=0.21, comfortably clear of the table, so either is a
# safe answer to "go home" / "回零点"; "safe" is the default because it is the
# pose this deploy actually boots into.
string target

# De-energise the arm's motors after it arrives ("失能", not "断电" — the
# drivers stay powered and the arm can be re-enabled without a restart).
# When true the pose move ALWAYS happens first: disabling in mid-air lets the
# arm sag under its own weight, which is why roboarm's own disconnect_arm()
# does reset -> move_to_home(safe_pos=True) -> disable_torque in that order.
bool disable
---
# Response

# Whether the arm reached the requested pose (and was disabled, if asked).
bool success

# Human-readable status.
string message

# How long the whole operation took (s).
float32 elapsed_s
